      "id": "e1",
      "title": "The alphabet and spelling your name",
      "body": "In Canada people ask you to spell your name all the time: on the phone with Service Canada, at a clinic, with a landlord, on a form. The French alphabet has the same 26 letters. Only the names of the letters are different. Learn them first, because everything else (names, emails, postal codes) uses them."
