      "type": "explain",
      "id": "e3",
      "title": "In Canada",
      "body": "In Canada the word for email is courriel. In France you hear mail or e-mail. For .ca say “point c-a” (point say-ah). Hyphens and dots are normal in names and addresses: say trait d'union and point."
    },
